{**
 * c-button - the one thing this page wants you to do, and the quieter things
 * beside it.
 *
 * A destination makes it a link and no destination makes it a button, because
 * the difference is what happens when it is used rather than how it looks. The
 * variant names a role - the quiet one is the alternative to the main action,
 * the danger one deletes or cancels something - rather than an appearance, so a
 * theme is free to draw any of them any way it likes.
 *
 * The small size is for a row of a table or a toolbar, where a button of the
 * page's size would make every row as tall as a heading. It is a size and not a
 * variant: a small button is still primary, quiet or danger.
 *
 * @param array<string, string|null> $attributes anything the caller has to hang
 *     on the control itself: a data- hook, an aria- relationship. The component
 *     adds none of its own, and a caller that needs one is not a reason to grow
 *     a parameter per attribute.
 * @param string|null $icon the name of a c-icon drawn after the label. The
 *     label still says what the control does, so the icon is decoration and is
 *     hidden from assistive technology.
 * @param bool $iconOnly draw the icon and nothing else. The label is still in
 *     the control, as text a screen reader reads and a translation reaches, and
 *     only hidden from the page; a control drawn this way without an icon would
 *     be a control with nothing on it, so it is refused.
 *}

{import 'icon.latte'}

{define button, string $label, string $href = '', string $variant = 'primary', ?string $testId = null, array $attributes = [], ?string $icon = null, string $size = 'default', bool $iconOnly = false}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::oneOf('c-button', 'variant', $variant, ['primary', 'quiet', 'danger'])}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::oneOf('c-button', 'size', $size, ['default', 'small'])}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::holds(
        !$iconOnly || $icon !== null,
        sprintf("c-button '%s' is to be drawn as only an icon and names no icon.", $label),
    )}

    {* One variant at a time, by construction: the class is made of the one
       variable, so no element can carry two variants deciding the same colours. *}
    <a
        n:tag="$href === '' ? 'button' : 'a'"
        n:class="
            'c-button',
            $variant !== 'primary' ? 'c-button--' . $variant,
            $size === 'small' ? 'c-button--small',
            $iconOnly ? 'c-button--icon-only'
        "
        n:attr="$attributes + ['href' => $href ?: null, 'type' => $href === '' ? 'button' : null, 'data-testid' => $testId]"
    >{if $iconOnly}<span class="u-visually-hidden">{$label}</span>{else}{$label}{/if}{if $icon !== null}{include icon, name: $icon}{/if}</a>
{/define}
